884 0 obj
  << /ActualText (WHAT I BRING\nBrand Identity \046 Brand Systems\nCreative Campaigns \046 Art Direction\nDigital\054 UX\057UI \046 Ecommerce Design\nCreative Artworking \046 Print Production\nTypography \046 Visual Storytelling\nAI\055Augmented Creative Workflows\nCreative Leadership \046 Mentoring\nStakeholder Collaboration \046 Pitching\nEnd\055to\055End Project Delivery\nAdobe Creative Cloud \046 Figma\nInternal and External Collaborations\n\nSELECTED CLIENTS\nPentland Brands\nSpeedo \057 Berghaus \057 Ellesse \057 Canterbury\nMitre \057 Kickers \057 Endura\nASSA ABLOY\nYale\nSomfy\nICI Dulux\n\nTOOLS\054 TECH \046 AI\nThe tools I use to make ideas real\054 and the ones I\047m exploring to make them faster\054 sharper\054 or just more interesting\056\nAdobe Creative Cloud\072\050Photoshop\054 Illustrator\054 InDesign\054 After Effects\nAI\072\050ChatGPT\054 Gemini\054 Firefly\054 Claude etc\nFigma\n\nWORKING STYLE\nI enjoy turning a good brief into great creative\054 and I\047m happiest working collaboratively \023 asking questions early and solving problems before they become obstacles\056\nColleagues know me as calm under pressure\054 honest about what\047s achievable\054 and always willing to roll up my sleeves\056 I\047m as interested in where design is going as where it\047s been\054 which is why I keep pulling new tools and techniques into how I work\056\n\nOUTSIDE DESIGN\nOutside of work I\031m usually found on a mountain bike\054 camping with the family\054 or building furniture in the garage\056 I like making things \023 timber\054 pixels or ideas\054 and that curiosity is exactly what keeps me excited about where design goes next\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 885 0 R
     /Pg 872 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
